    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Freeman** (72.25) leads the LawDog offense, benefiting from an elite park factor and a favorable matchup against a lefty with a pedestrian 4.32 xERA. His role in the two-hole provides the optimal environment for run production. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94), **Luis Arraez** (68.94), and **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.73) present high-floor value against the right-handed pitching trio of Kochanowicz and Gordon. **Jung Hoo Lee**, in particular, benefits significantly from the \"Slow SP Delivery\" multiplier, making him a primary target for stolen base potential today. While **Daulton Varsho** (55.65) faces a tougher test against the 3.09 xERA of Bradish, he remains a viable start due to a massive park-factor boost that compensates for the challenging pitching matchup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Bryson Stott** (51.43). While **Bryson Stott** projected well against Yamamoto, he fell just short of the efficiency thresholds held by **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Drew Gilbert**. The optimizer prioritized the specific speed-based advantages inherent in the active lineup\u2019s matchups against slow-working pitchers, whereas **Bryson Stott** was dinged by the \"Elite Hold SP\" penalty associated with his opposition. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding **Daulton Varsho** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who face pitchers capable of stifling production; both have been flagged for the 60% SB-prevention rate of their respective matchups. As always, we are closely monitoring the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while keeping our depth pieces like **Taylor Ward** and **Masyn Winn** ready should any late-scratch lineup shifts require a pivot.",
